        "title": "Pelagic Zone and Open Ocean Ecology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The open ocean (pelagic zone) covers ~65% of Earth's surface and constitutes ~99% of\nEarth's inhabitable volume by space. Most of it appears blue and empty but is actually a\ncomplex three-tier system: primary producers at the surface, a global carbon export pump\ndriven by sinking particles, and a microbial loop recycling most of the carbon before it\nleaves the photic zone."
